phase P4
title Preview
description
    **Class:** not readily verifiable.

    **Kind:** verification-suite.

    **Goal:** the preview cut the user named (2026-11-12): the fixtures, including Pay and checkout, in real Chrome and
    Safari through a minimal React binding and IndexedDB; the rest of the core's slices (fragments, reads and
    operations, release versions); `flow check`; and `nub run verify` building v3.

    **Starts when:** P3's completion audit passes.

    **Verified by:**

    - a real-browser run of the fixtures, whose driver and checks @task.V3.T58 builds and proves first; it runs alone;
    - for the core slices, the same suite as P3: Story tests, run rules and compile-time tests from each Spec, with a
      planted fault for each new rule in code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts;
    - skill:check-task per Task; skill:check-runtime in the real browsers; `nub run check` at zero.

    **One iteration:** the next ready Task: its Spec change, its requirements as failing checks, the code, an
    independent skill:check-task. The user's page is written at each slice's close.

    **Exit criteria:**

    - every Task is done;
    - the fixtures run in real Chrome and Safari, and a fault planted in the browser path is caught there;
    - `nub run verify` passes and builds `packages/flow-state-v3`;
    - the suite's coverage record is updated, and an audit by a lead that did not build the suite has
      passed (skill:policy-testing#audit-a-suite);
    - the completion audit names each Plan outcome these Tasks satisfy and finds it delivered.

    **False pass:** a browser run that passes on a fake store or a fake page.

    **Caught by:** skill:check-runtime on the real interface, and a planted fault in the IndexedDB path.

    **Gates:**

    - `nub run faults`, which rejects the dead core and the named faults in code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts;
    - the browser run, which rejects its own planted fault (built by @task.V3.T58);
    - `nub run verify`.

    **Failure limit:** none (the user, 2026-11-22): a repeated root cause is recorded on the slice's Tasks and the run
    goes on (@epic.V3, Limits).

    **Stops:**

    - a guarantee that can't be met;
    - public entry-point names or a large public API change.

    **User's read:** each Spec revision; small public API calls; the user's page at each slice's close.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:policy-verification and skill:policy-testing, as in P3;
    - skill:check-runtime for the browser run;
    - skill:to-spec and skill:to-design per module; skill:execute-task and skill:check-task per Task;
    - skill:review at a Task's first commit and its close.

    **Order:** @task.V3.T131, @task.V3.T120 (slice parent @task.V3.T89), @task.V3.T118, the typed-machine slice
    (@task.V3.T142: @task.V3.T113, @task.V3.T143, @task.V3.T144), @task.V3.T119, @task.V3.T92, @task.V3.T21's children
    @task.V3.T121 to @task.V3.T124, @task.V3.T56, the Fragments slice (@task.V3.T133: @task.V3.T109, @task.V3.T110), the
    channels slice (@task.V3.T77: @task.V3.T127, @task.V3.T76, @task.V3.T128), the UI slice (@task.V3.T72:
    @task.V3.T129, @task.V3.T130, @task.V3.T78, @task.V3.T73), the Errors and CLI slice (@task.V3.T134: @task.V3.T22,
    @task.V3.T100, @task.V3.T23); the host track after @task.V3.T119: Host A (@task.V3.T135: @task.V3.T112,
    @task.V3.T111), Host B (@task.V3.T136: @task.V3.T97, @task.V3.T117). [decided: user 2026-11-22] Why: the algorithm
    designs put the typed machine, the turn walk and the records first, and every slice after them. Reverse: the order
    of the breakdown review (the orchestrator, 2026-11-20). A `blocked_by` link is a real dependency only; where several
    Tasks are ready, take the earliest in this order.

    Every Task below is a draft. Before starting its lead, the orchestrator writes its full text with skill:to-task. The
    earlier text of each, in `wiki/tasks/V3/` at commit `6b9fe478`, was written for the conformance suite: it is
    background only, and its acceptance does not carry over. The suite's coverage record is the one @task.V3.T67 starts;
    the browser run adds its own entry to it.
