    T95
        title           Callback results checked before they enter a turn
        status          tombstone
        priority        high
        satisfies       [@plan.Runtime.O5]
        description
            Every user callback's result is checked before it enters a turn: an `updateMemory` patch by its keys and
            each field's Schema, an ending mapper's payload by its event's check.

            **Why now:** found while drafting the boundary map: `updateMemory`'s patch is spread outside its `call`
            (code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/walk.ts#accept), so its keys and values are trusted, and an ending
            mapper's payload enters the turn unchecked against its event
            (code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/serve.ts). It is the "user callback results" row of the boundary map,
            the one source with no owner.

            **Read first:** @convention.boundaries, @spec.Turn, @spec.Diagnostics, @spec.Codec (R6).

            **Risk:** checking patch values walks large patches twice: the palette's `Configure` patches 100,000
            commands. The bench decides whether production checks values or only keys (dev and test always check both).

            **Approach:** red first, a Story per gap (an unknown patch key, a patch value its field's Schema refuses, a
            mapper payload its event refuses); then one callback wrapper keeping the cause and slot replaces `call`
            (core/turn.ts) and `callSlot` (core/compiled.ts), with the result check inside it.

            Design first (the user, 2026-11-19, after T92): before the per-check list, the requirements ask whether a
            structure removes the class, so a callback result can't enter a turn unchecked by construction (one wrapper
            every callback passes through, results decoded by the slot's Schema), rather than adding checks one by one;
            the first commit states the choice and why.

            Fixtures: no catalog step; the refusals are edge values for @convention.fixtures (hostile patches and mapper
            payloads in the fixtures' step samples, the palette's large patch as load). The raw-throw class stays parked
            in @task.V3.T98.

            May change: `src/core/`, `tests/`, `fixtures/`, @spec.Turn and @spec.Diagnostics with `specs.log` notes.
            Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a check that runs in dev but not in the host the Story uses → caught by the Story asserting the
            refusal under the stress profile. Gates: `nub run faults --only` on its planted faults `patch-unchecked` and
            `mapper-payload-unchecked`, each caught by its named test; the palette bench, `nub run bench --only
            scale.command-palette.list-length-100000.per-turn-ms --dev`, before and after. User's read: whether
            production checks patch values, from the bench.
        acceptance
            - An unknown patch key, a patch value its field's Schema refuses and a mapper payload its event refuses each
              refuse the turn with a FlowError naming the slot, shown red first by a Story test.
            - One callback wrapper keeps the thrown cause and slot; `call` and `callSlot` are gone.
            - Fixtures first (@convention.fixtures): the hostile patch and payload samples are in the fixtures' step
              samples and run by every runner before the build; the proof is posted as a Task comment.
            - The palette's per-turn median grows by at most 10 % with checks on, or production checks keys only,
              recorded with the bench numbers.
            - `nub run check`, the suite and stress pass; `nub run faults --only` catches this Task's planted faults.
        deletion_reason
            Cut (the user, 2026-11-19): no wrong ending it would prevent; TypeScript covers callback result shapes,
            operation contracts decode outside data at the boundary, and capture encodes memory through its Schema
            (UnencodableValue at write). Its routed items moved to @task.V3.T99 and @task.V3.T57.

    T96
        title       Actor-to-actor send(ref, event) action with the loop guard
        status      done
        priority    high


        satisfies   [@plan.Runtime.O4]
        description
            A machine sends a public event to another actor with a `send(toRef, toEvent)` action, delivered as a later
            turn of the target, with the loop guard that bounds a chain of sends.

            **Why now:** the user's decision (2026-11-18, re-plan Q4 A). Host code is the only way one actor reaches
            another today, which Stories and `flow check` can't see; step-1 fixture cells in pay, sync, transfers,
            palette and player wait on it. The Plans already specify it: @plan.Runtime.O4 (the send table by target),
            @plan.LazyFeatures (a send never adopts), Actors R13 and I20 (the loop guard, built with the action).

            **Read first:** @plan.Runtime.O4, @spec.Actors (R13, I20), @epic.V3 (re-plan section 7, Q4
            A), @convention.boundaries.

            **Risk:** two machines that send to each other import each other's Machine for the ref; this Task checks
            whether a ref by definition is needed, and that is a public API call for the user.

            **Approach:** `send` is a builder: it captures its two callbacks unread; `machine()` decodes it as an
            action. At run time the event goes through the target's event check, the same one a handle's `send` runs
            (the target's events aren't in the sender's types, so this check prevents a wrong ending); the ref is a
            Flow-made value, typed by TypeScript. T95 was cut (the user, 2026-11-19): no general callback wrapper, and
            every check names the wrong ending it prevents. Delivery follows O4's table: never creates, never adopts,
            may restore. The guard: past `RuntimeDefaults.loopGuard` events sent by turns from one admitted event, the
            turn that would send one more is refused `InvalidTurn` naming the chain; context updates never count (D13).
            Listener-originated chains (Actors Q4) stay as they are.

            May change: `src/`, `tests/`, `fixtures/`, @spec.Actors with a `specs.log` note. Evidence: this
            Task's comments.

            False pass: a guard that counts but never refuses → caught by a ping-pong Story past the guard that must end
            refused. Gates: `nub run faults --only` on its planted faults `send-creates-target`, `send-adopts-lazy` and
            `loop-guard-off`, each caught by its named test. Stops: a public API change beyond `send(toRef, toEvent)` (a
            ref by definition). User's read: the send's final signature.
        acceptance
            - `send(toRef, toEvent)` delivers by every row of @plan.Runtime.O4's send table, each row a Story in
              a fixture.
            - The waiting step-1 cells in shop, sync and player use it and pass (amended 2026-11-19: transfers and
              palette cut by the orchestrator's ruling, transfers because its machine takes no input, Actors R5).
            - A chain past `RuntimeDefaults.loopGuard` is refused `InvalidTurn` naming the admitted event, the count
              shared by every consumer its context updates reach; a context update chain is not.
            - A send's target ref and event are checked; a bad one refuses the sender's turn `InvalidTurn` (amended
              2026-11-19: the refusal is InvalidTurn, not a FlowError, by the close review).
            - `nub run check`, the suite and stress pass; `nub run faults --only` catches this Task's planted faults.
        comment     2026-11-19T06:53:03Z
