    T141
        title       Bench loads again: the testing entry imports no test runner
        status      done
        priority    high
        description
            The bench loads and records again: nothing the fixtures import pulls in the test runner at load time.

            **Why now:** `nub run bench tooling --record` fails before running anything (`benches/index.ts did not load:
            'vite-plus/test' does not provide an export named 'describe'`). The fixtures import
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/testing/index.ts, which re-exports `storeContract`;
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/testing/store-contract.ts imports `describe`, `expect` and `it` from
            `vite-plus/test` at module load. Under `nub run`, nub applies the root tsconfig's `paths`, which map that
            specifier to a declarations-only file, so the import is empty there (plain node loads the real vitest).
            Broken since @task.V3.T58 added it (2026-11-20); the last bench rows are from 2026-11-18 and 2026-11-19, so
            T120, T131 and T140 landed unmeasured.

            **Read first:** @convention.bench;
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/bench/list.ts; code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/testing/store-contract.ts.

            **Build-time choice:** A: `storeContract` takes the runner's `describe` and `it` as an argument, so loading
            the testing entry imports no runner. B: `storeContract` moves to its own testing entry that fixtures never
            import. A keeps one public testing entry and changes one call; B adds a public entry name, which is a phase
            stop. Resolving the runner lazily inside the call is out: a dynamic import is async, and `describe` must
            register while the file is collected. Test: code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/bench/load.test.ts, which
            loads `fixtures/index.ts` and `bench/` under nub, as the bench runner does, and records every runner import;
            pick the option that passes it with the smaller public change, and tag it.

            **Risk:** `storeContract` is public test tooling, used by the IndexedDB adapter's browser tests; its call
            shape for users must stay readable.

            May change: `packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/testing/`, `bench/`, `tests/`, `tools/browser/`.
        acceptance
