        comment     2026-11-22T08:47:35Z
            Root cause (builder): nub applies tsconfig `paths` at run time, and `tsconfig.base.json` maps
            `vite-plus/test` to the declarations-only `types/vite-plus-test.d.ts`, so under `nub run bench` the import
            becomes an empty module. The trigger is code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/testing/store-contract.ts, the
            only non-test module reachable from `fixtures/index.ts` that imports the runner (`describe`, `expect`, `it`)
            at load. `run.ts` and `list.ts` are not at fault: `node bench/run.ts --list` and `nub run --node bench
            --list` load; `nub run bench --list` fails.

            - Origin: nub 0.7.5's preload (`~/.cache/nub/runtime-0.7.5-*/transform-core.mjs`, "the ADDITIVE TS
              resolution — tsconfig `paths` aliases") resolves before Node. Installed `vite-plus` 1.7.0 `./test` is
              `export * from 'vitest'` (vitest 5.1.0 `dist/index.js`, which exports `describe`); plain node takes
              that path.
            - Workers inherit it: code:packages/flow-state-v3/bench/workers.ts#spawnWorker spawns `process.execPath`
              with the parent's env, so its `NODE_OPTIONS` (nub's `--require preload.cjs`) too.
            - `--dev` does not load either: `nub run bench --only turn.cells.long.per-turn-ms --dev` exits 1 with the
              same `did not load`. The T118 dev rows can't have come from `nub run bench` at this tree.

            Two traces, one resolve hook recording runner imports, importing `fixtures/index.ts`
            and `src/host/testing/index.ts`:

            ```text
            node:  runner  vite-plus/test <- src/host/testing/store-contract.ts
                           vitest <- node_modules/vite-plus/dist/test/index.js
                   failed  none          (loads, but pulls the whole vitest graph into the process)
            nub:   resolve vite-plus/test -> types/vite-plus-test.d.ts   (node: node_modules/vite-plus/dist/test/index.js)
                   runner  vite-plus/test <- src/host/testing/store-contract.ts
                   failed  fixtures/index.ts, testing/index.ts: 'vite-plus/test' does not provide an export named 'describe'
            ```

            Which side is wrong: Flow's code. A runner-agnostic testing entry needs the runner at load: under plain node
            it loads vitest into every bench worker, and fails for a user with no vitest. The `paths` shim only turns
            that into a load error; it is root tooling outside this Task and stays, and the load guard catches any later
            runner import it would break.
